Que 1) Concurrent Hashmap internal working ?
---------------------------------------------
When we create an object of ConcurrentHashMap in Java, 16 buckets are not created immediately. 
The table is created lazily when the first entry is added (default capacity is 16).
When we add an entry:
First it calculates hashCode
Then it calculates index value using that hash
Based on index, entry is assigned to a particular bucket in Node format
If bucket is null:
Entry is inserted using CAS (no locking required)
If bucket is not null:
It will lock only that particular bucket (not whole map)
Then it checks:
If key already exists → value is updated
If key not exists → entry is added in linked list
After operation completes:
Lock is automatically released (no manual unlock)
If more than 8 entries are present in the same bucket:
Linked list is converted into tree structure (Red-Black Tree)
(only if table size ≥ 64, otherwise resizing happens)

