Que 3) How to use Employee object as key in HashMap? 
----------------------------------------------------
In Java, if you want to use a custom object (like Employee) as a key in HashMap, you must override:
👉 hashCode()
👉 equals()
🔹 Why Required?
HashMap internally uses:
hashCode() → to find bucket
equals() → to compare keys inside bucket
❗ If you don’t override:
Duplicate keys may be inserted
Retrieval may fail ==> We will get null values 

Que 4) Diff between @Primary and @Component ?
---------------------------------------------
When you have multiple beans of same type, Spring gets confused:
@Component
class Car {}
@Component
class Bike {}
@Autowired
Vehicle vehicle; // ❌ Error: multiple beans
👉 This is called NoUniqueBeanDefinitionException
🔹 2. @Primary
👉 Default bean choose karne ke liye
@Component
@Primary
class Car implements Vehicle {}
@Component
class Bike implements Vehicle {}
@Autowired
Vehicle vehicle;
👉 Output:
Car bean injected ✅
✔ Spring automatically selects @Primary bean
🔹 3. @Qualifier
👉 Specific bean choose karne ke liye
@Component("carBean")
class Car implements Vehicle {}
@Component("bikeBean")
class Bike implements Vehicle {}
@Autowired
@Qualifier("bikeBean")
Vehicle vehicle;
👉 Output:
Bike bean injected ✅
✔ You explicitly tell Spring which bean to use
🔥 Key Differences
Feature	@Primary	@Qualifier
Purpose	Default selection	Specific selection
Usage	Class level	Field/parameter level
Control	Less	More precise
When used	When 1 bean should be default	When multiple choices needed

Que 5)What is ExecutorService?
In Java, ExecutorService is used to manage and control multiple threads.
👉 Instead of creating threads manually, it:
Creates a thread pool
Reuses threads
Executes tasks efficiently
🔹 Why use it?
✔ Better performance
✔ Thread reuse
✔ Controlled execution
🔹 Types of ExecutorService
Using Executors class:
1. Fixed Thread Pool
Executors.newFixedThreadPool(5);
👉 Fixed number of threads
2. Cached Thread Pool
Executors.newCachedThreadPool();
👉 Creates threads as needed, reuses old ones
3. Single Thread Executor
Executors.newSingleThreadExecutor();
👉 Only one thread (sequential execution)
4. Scheduled Thread Pool
Executors.newScheduledThreadPool(3);
👉 Runs tasks after delay or periodically

Que 6) When concurrent modification exception occured ?
In Java, ConcurrentModificationException occurs when a collection is structurally modified (add/remove) while it 
is being iterated using a fail-fast iterator (like for-each or Iterator), except through the iterator’s own remove() method.
